Article 14 The use of radio frequencies shall be subject to licensing, except for the following frequencies:
(1) Frequencies used by amateur radio stations, public walkie-talkies, and standard radio stations;
(2) International safety and distress systems, international fixed frequencies used for aeronautical and maritime mobile services and radio navigation services;
(3) Frequencies used by micro-power short-range radio transmitting equipment as prescribed by the national radio regulatory authority.

Article 15 To obtain a radio frequency use license, the following conditions shall be met:
(1) The applied radio frequency complies with the regulations on radio frequency allocation and use, and has a clear and specific purpose;
(2) The technical scheme for using the radio frequency is feasible;
(3) There are corresponding professional technical personnel;
(4) No harmful interference will be caused to other radio frequencies used according to law.

Article 27 The establishment and use of a radio station (or station) shall be subject to applying to the radio regulatory authority for obtaining a radio station license, except for the establishment and use of the following radio stations:
(1) terrestrial public mobile communication terminals;
(2) receive-only radio stations;
(3) micro-power short-distance radio stations as prescribed by the national radio regulatory authority.

Article 28 Except for amateur radio stations specified in Article 29 of these Regulations, the establishment and use of a radio station (or station) shall meet the following conditions:
(1) having available radio frequencies;
(2) the radio transmitting equipment used has legally obtained a radio transmitting equipment type approval certificate and meets the product quality requirements prescribed by the State;
(3) having personnel familiar with radio management provisions and possessing relevant professional skills;
(4) having clear and specific purposes and a feasible technical solution;
(5) having an electromagnetic environment that can ensure the normal use of the radio station (or station), and the intended radio station (or station) shall not cause harmful interference to other radio stations (or stations) legally in use.
An application for establishing and using a space radio station shall, in addition to meeting the conditions set forth in the preceding paragraph, also have available satellite radio frequencies and satellite orbital resources.

To obtain type approval for radio transmission equipment, the following conditions shall be met:
(1) The applicant has corresponding production capacity, technical capability, and quality assurance system;
(2) The technical specifications such as operating frequency and power of the radio transmission equipment comply with national standards and relevant provisions on national radio administration.

Article 72 Anyone who, in violation of these Regulations, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the radio regulatory authority to make corrections, and his illegal gains shall be confiscated, and a fine of not more than 30,000 yuan may also be imposed; if serious consequences are caused, his radio station license shall be revoked, and a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall also be imposed:
(1) Setting up or using a radio station (station) not in accordance with the licensed matters and requirements specified in the radio station license;
(2) Deliberately transmitting and receiving radio signals beyond the licensed matters of the radio station license, or disseminating, publishing, or making use of inadvertently received information;
(3) Compiling or using a radio station identification code without authorization.

Article 75 Anyone who, in violation of these Regulations, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the radio regulatory authority to make corrections; if he refuses to make corrections, the equipment used for the illegal activities shall be confiscated, and a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed; if serious consequences are caused, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan shall also be imposed:
(1) Developing, producing, selling, or repairing high-power radio transmitting equipment without taking effective measures to suppress radio wave transmission;
(2) A foreign organization or individual conducting radio wave parameter testing or radio wave monitoring within the territory of China;
(3) Providing domestic radio wave parameter data involving national security to a foreign organization or individual.
